From: GL-MT6000 fork <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] interface: make the ingress ifb multiqueue so cake_mq attaches

With the "multiqueue" option enabled qosify emits "root cake_mq" for the
ingress qdisc too, but that qdisc runs on the ifb created by
cmd_add_ingress(), which is created with a single tx queue.  cake_mq
refuses to attach to a single-queue device:

  qosify: Command: tc qdisc add dev 'ifb-eth1' root cake_mq ...
  qosify: RTNETLINK answers: Not supported

so the ifb silently falls back to the default "fq" root and ingress
shaping is a no-op.

Create the ifb with one tx queue per online CPU when multiqueue is set,
so cake_mq can spread flows across queues (see the matching
ifb_select_queue() helper in the kernel tree).

Signed-off-by: GL-MT6000 fork <noreply@localhost>
---
 interface.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/interface.c b/interface.c
--- a/interface.c
+++ b/interface.c
@@ -344,7 +344,23 @@
 	if (!iface->config.ingress)
 		return 0;
 
-	snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "ip link add '%s' type ifb", ifbdev);
+	/*
+	 * cake_mq only attaches to multiqueue devices.  The ingress qdisc
+	 * runs on the ifb created here; with a single tx queue cake_mq
+	 * fails with "RTNETLINK answers: Not supported" and the ifb root
+	 * falls back to fq.  Give the ifb one tx queue per CPU so cake_mq
+	 * can spread flows across them.
+	 */
+	if (iface->config.multiqueue) {
+		long nq = sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN);
+		if (nq < 2)
+			nq = 2;
+		snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf),
+			 "ip link add name '%s' numtxqueues %ld type ifb",
+			 ifbdev, nq);
+	} else {
+		snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "ip link add '%s' type ifb", ifbdev);
+	}
 	qosify_run_cmd(buf, false);
 
 	cmd_add_qdisc(iface, ifbdev, false, eth);
